{"c":[{"id":"686710946312e7ea","sum":"Chrome ignores native AX writes once web AX is on (HostCoordinator yields via PageInline.nativeYields); PageTaskMachine.publish invalidates its live offer first. H14 rig: no guest Jev, use 'pagetask start'; banners cover top-right panels.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"806a636804d6e5d8","sum":"Chrome page fields: once web AX is on, Chrome ignores native AX writes (HostCoordinator yields via PageInline.nativeYields); PageTaskMachine.publish invalidates its own live offer before republishing, or onDisplaced drops the page task.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T172603Z-a7ca0252d9058e55","text":"Once an assistive app turns on Chrome's web accessibility, native ghost text sees page fields, but Chrome ignores its AX writes (writeIgnored): Tab is eaten. HostCoordinator yields to page inline text via PageInline.nativeYields.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T211151Z-05df8b8f447e91f6","text":"H14: PageTaskMachine.publish must invalidate its own live offer before republishing (a click changes the preview without a key): otherwise the arbiter's onDisplaced puts the whole page task away.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cfa933fb97832a8e","sum":"H14 rig: guest has no Jev; drive attach rows with hook 'pagetask start <goalProgress>' (pageTask.lastAccept* shows Tab). Banners cover top-right panels: give canned page goals a lower viewport. clickableContent panels need a mouse move before a click.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T211204Z-63399dc84dfcee60","text":"H14: the rig guest has no Jev, so an Ask gives no page goal; drive attach rows with test hook 'pagetask start <goalProgress>'. The helper echoes no goalAccept: state pageTask.lastAccept* shows what Tab sent.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T211204Z-f2f5d457e6044752","text":"H14: macOS notification banners cover Caret's panels at the screen's top right; a rig click there hits the banner. Give canned page goals a viewport lower down. clickableContent panels take a click only after a mouse move over them.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ca6b56f177286a70","sum":"Live Jev: run sets once (43-81 requests/pass); HOIST_SHARED_OPTIONS false (LV1). W1: offline guard-adversary.ts each batch, class (a) writes 0; labelled lines offer parts. All chosen writes use fill/writable.ts writeMisfit; add rules there; candidates added, never swapped.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"99b0cde49d41360f","sum":"Live Jev: run live sets once (R1's slow-eval never settles; each pass sends 43-81 new requests). Keep HOIST_SHARED_OPTIONS false: on, Jev answered 'none' on names and emails on four small forms (LV1 compare-hoist.txt).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T015102Z-70f8faec6a3a0648","text":"R1's slow-eval runner never settles on live Jev: each pass sends 43-81 new requests, so a set costs about 3x one pass. Run live sets once.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T015102Z-cf129cc10068e635","text":"HOIST_SHARED_OPTIONS changes Jev's answers: with it on, Jev answered 'none' on names and emails on four small forms. Keep it false (LV1 compare-hoist.txt).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"5678229122db2693","sum":"W1: run helper/scripts/guard-adversary.ts offline each batch; class (a) writes must stay 0. Labelled multi-value lines offer parts, not whole lines. All chosen-value writes use fill/writable.ts writeMisfit; add rules there. Candidates are added, never swapped.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T020955Z-5dafeedfea56fda2","text":"W1: canned evals never pick a plausible wrong candidate; run helper/scripts/guard-adversary.ts (offline, ~2 s) each batch: class (a) writes must stay 0. A labelled multi-value line offers its parts, not its whole (line-values severalValues).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T025421Z-86d442b2d62eead8","text":"Any path that writes a chosen value into a field checks fill/writable.ts writeMisfit (fill, planner validate, codeplan, offer filter, goal gate); add new value rules there, not beside one caller. Candidates are only added, never swapped out.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
